### Ansible Standards

#### 1. Role Structure

```yaml
# roles/<role-name>/
# ├── tasks/
# │   └── main.yml        # Primary tasks
# ├── handlers/
# │   └── main.yml        # Handlers
# ├── defaults/
# │   └── main.yml        # Default variables
# ├── vars/
# │   └── main.yml        # Role variables
# ├── templates/
# │   └── config.j2       # Jinja2 templates
# ├── files/
# ├── meta/
# │   └── main.yml        # Role metadata
# └── README.md
```

#### 2. Task Writing Standards

```yaml
# ✅ Good: Descriptive name, tags, check mode support
- name: CIS 1.1.1 | Disable unused filesystems
  copy:
    dest: /etc/modprobe.d/cis.conf
    content: |
      install cramfs /bin/true
    mode: '0644'
    owner: root
    group: root
  tags:
    - cis
    - filesystem
    - level1
  check_mode: yes

# ❌ Bad: No name, no tags, fails in check mode
- copy:
    dest: /etc/modprobe.d/cis.conf
    content: "install cramfs /bin/true"
```

#### 3. Idempotency Requirements

```yaml
# ✅ Good: Idempotent (safe to run multiple times)
- name: Ensure SSH is configured securely
  lineinfile:
    path: /etc/ssh/sshd_config
    regexp: '^#?PermitRootLogin'
    line: 'PermitRootLogin no'
    validate: '/usr/sbin/sshd -t -f %s'
  notify: restart sshd

# ❌ Bad: Not idempotent (appends every run)
- name: Configure SSH
  shell: echo "PermitRootLogin no" >> /etc/ssh/sshd_config
```

#### 4. Variable Naming

```yaml
# defaults/main.yml
---
# Role-specific prefix
cis_hardening_level: 2
cis_disable_ipv6: true
cis_enable_auditd: true

# Global variables (from inventory)
cluster_name: "{{ lookup('env', 'CLUSTER_NAME') }}"
environment: "{{ lookup('env', 'ENVIRONMENT') }}"
```

