## 🔐 Security & Compliance

### Security Checklist

**Before submitting PR**:

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets (use AWS Secrets Manager, Vault)
- [ ] No sensitive data in logs or outputs
- [ ] All resources encrypted at rest (KMS)
- [ ] All resources encrypted in transit (TLS 1.2+)
- [ ] IAM roles follow least-privilege principle
- [ ] Security groups follow default-deny principle
- [ ] Container images from approved registries only
- [ ] No privileged containers (unless Security Pod approved)
- [ ] All pods have resource limits
- [ ] NetworkPolicies defined for new namespaces

### Compliance Scanning

```bash
# Run all compliance checks
make compliance-check

# Includes:
# - CIS Kubernetes Benchmark (kube-bench)
# - PCI-DSS controls
# - SOC2 requirements
# - FIPS 140-3 validation
```

### Secrets Management

**✅ Approved Methods**:

```hcl
# Terraform: Use AWS Secrets Manager
data "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "api_key" {
  secret_id = "prod/api/key"
}

# Kubernetes: Use External Secrets Operator
apiVersion: external-secrets.io/v1beta1
kind: ExternalSecret
metadata:
  name: database-credentials
spec:
  secretStoreRef:
    name: vault-backend
    kind: SecretStore
  target:
    name: database-credentials
  data:
    - secretKey: password
      remoteRef:
        key: database/prod/credentials
        property: password
```

**❌ Never Do This**:

```hcl
# Hardcoded secrets
variable "api_key" {
  default = "sk-abc123..."  # CRITICAL SECURITY VIOLATION
}

# Secrets in Git
resource "aws_db_instance" "main" {
  password = "SuperSecret123!"  # CRITICAL SECURITY VIOLATION
}
```

