## 👀 Review Process

### PR Requirements

**All PRs must have**:

1. **Descriptive title** following conventional commits
2. **Clear description** explaining:
   - What changed and why
   - How to test
   - Any risks or breaking changes
3. **Linked issue** (Jira ticket or GitHub issue)
4. **Test evidence** (screenshots, logs, terraform plan output)
5. **Documentation updates** (if applicable)
6. **Cost impact** (if infrastructure change)

### Review Checklist

**Reviewers must verify**:

- [ ] Code follows standards (see sections above)
- [ ] All tests pass (CI/CD pipeline green)
- [ ] Security scan clean (no HIGH/CRITICAL findings)
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No secrets in code
- [ ] Resource tagging complete
- [ ] Tested in non-prod environment
- [ ] Rollback plan documented (for production changes)

### Approval Requirements

| Change Type | Approvals Required | Auto-Deploy |
|-------------|-------------------|-------------|
| **Hotfix** (production issue) | 1 architect | Yes (after approval) |
| **Feature** (new functionality) | 1 peer + 1 architect | No (manual) |
| **Refactor** (no functional change) | 1 peer | Yes (nonprod only) |
| **Documentation** | 1 peer | Yes |
| **Breaking Change** | 2 architects + VP approval | No (manual) |

